{"schema":"plectis_maths_universe_excerpts_v1","paper":"erdos-257-mersenne-support-subseries","excerpts":[["statement:erdos-257-mersenne-support-subseries#res:cylinderhalf","unbounded shared-prefix families\nrepresent one half","<p><em> Suppose that for every <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>N</mi></math></span> there are <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>M</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>K</mi></math></span> with <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mo movablelimits=\"true\">max</mo><mo fence=\"false\" stretchy=\"false\">{</mo><mi>N</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo fence=\"false\" stretchy=\"false\">}</mo><mo>≤</mo><mi>M</mi></math></span>, <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>K</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>M</mi></math></span>, and a family satisfying all\nthe conditions in the preceding paragraph. Then <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></math></span> for some infinite set <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>A</mi><mo>⊆</mo><msub><mrow><mi>ℕ</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub></math></span>.</em></p>"],["statement:erdos-257-mersenne-support-subseries#res:general-repair","membership and nonincreasing integer\nremainders","<p><em> For every real <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>x</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></math></span>, the following are equivalent:\n</em></p>\n<div class=\"math-display\"><span class=\"math display\"><math display=\"block\"><mtable displaystyle=\"true\" columnspacing=\"1em\" rowspacing=\"3pt\" data-break-align=\"middle\" minlabelspacing=\"0em\"><mtr><mtd><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>𝒜</mi></mrow><mo>;</mo></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">∀</mi><mi>K</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn><mtext> </mtext><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">∃</mi><mi>N</mi><mo>≥</mo><mi>K</mi><mo>:</mo><mspace width=\"1em\"></mspace><msub><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo>;</mo></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">∀</mi><mi>K</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn><mtext> </mtext><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">∃</mi><mi>N</mi><mo>∈</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">[</mo><mi>K</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>K</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mo fence=\"false\" stretchy=\"false\">⌊</mo><msqrt><mi>K</mi></msqrt><mo fence=\"false\" stretchy=\"false\">⌋</mo><mo>+</mo><mn>12</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>:</mo><mspace width=\"1em\"></mspace><msub><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo>.</mo></mtd></mtr></mtable></math></span></div>"],["statement:erdos-257-mersenne-support-subseries#res:mixed-supports","mixed weighted and cover supports","<p><em>\nLet <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>E</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>V</mi><mo>⊆</mo><msub><mrow><mi>ℕ</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub></math></span>. Suppose\n<span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>E</mi></math></span> satisfies <a class=\"math-ref\" data-equation-ref=\"true\" href=\"papers/erdos-257-mersenne-support-subseries.html#eq:weighted-return\">(W)</a> for a finite\nnonempty prime set <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>P</mi></math></span>, and <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>V</mi><mo>⊆</mo><munder><mo>⋃</mo><mi>j</mi></munder><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></math></span> for finite sets\nand nonnegative majorants satisfying the hypotheses of Theorem <a class=\"math-ref\" href=\"papers/erdos-257-mersenne-support-subseries.html#thm:variable-fractional-cover\" data-universe-ref=\"statement:erdos-257-mersenne-support-subseries#thm:variable-fractional-cover\">3.1</a>, with\neither <a class=\"math-ref\" data-equation-ref=\"true\" href=\"papers/erdos-257-mersenne-support-subseries.html#eq:strengthened-cover\">(V)</a> or its\npositive-weight variant. Then <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></math></span> is irrational for every infinite\n<span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>A</mi><mo>⊆</mo><mi>E</mi><mo>∪</mo><mi>V</mi></math></span> and every\ninteger <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>b</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>2</mn></math></span>.</em></p>"],["statement:erdos-257-mersenne-support-subseries#res:one-over-twenty-one-frontier","integer-quotient tests for <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>21</mn></math></span>","<p><em> The following statements\nhold.</em></p>\n<ol>\n<li><p><em><span class=\"math inline\"><math><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>21</mn><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>𝒜</mi></mrow></math></span> if and\nonly if <span class=\"math inline\"><math><msub><mrow><mi>ℱ</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>21</mn></mrow></msub></math></span> does not\nhold.</em></p></li>\n<li><p><em>If there is an unbounded sequence of ranks <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>R</mi></math></span> with <span class=\"math inline\"><math><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mi>R</mi></msup></math></span>, then <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>21</mn><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>𝒜</mi></mrow></math></span>.</em></p></li>\n<li><p><em>On <span class=\"math inline\"><math><msub><mrow><mi>ℱ</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>21</mn></mrow></msub></math></span>,\neventually <span class=\"math inline\"><math><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mi>R</mi></msup></math></span>, the boundary\nrank <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>R</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></math></span> belongs to <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><msub><mi>D</mi><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></math></span>, and, for all sufficiently large\n<span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>R</mi></math></span>, </em></p>\n<div class=\"math-display\"><span\nclass=\"math display\"><math display=\"block\"><mtable displaystyle=\"true\" columnalign=\"right left\" columnspacing=\"0em\" rowspacing=\"3pt\" data-break-align=\"bottom top\" minlabelspacing=\"0em\"><mtr><mtd><msub><mi>D</mi><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mtd><mtd><mstyle indentshift=\"2em\"><mi></mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><mo>∪</mo><mo fence=\"false\" stretchy=\"false\">{</mo><mi>R</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo fence=\"false\" stretchy=\"false\">}</mo><mo>,</mo></mstyle></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mtd><mtd><mstyle indentshift=\"2em\"><mi></mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo>⌊</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>R</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace=\"0.278em\" rspace=\"0.278em\">mod</mo><mn>21</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow><mn>21</mn></mfrac><mo>⌋</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn><msub><mi>c</mi><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>R</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>R</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>R</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>R</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mstyle></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd><mstyle indentshift=\"2em\"><mi></mi><mspace width=\"3em\"></mspace><mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>.</mo></mstyle></mtd></mtr></mtable></math></span></div>\n<p><em> Here <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><msub><mi>c</mi><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>R</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">#</mi><mo fence=\"false\" stretchy=\"false\">{</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><mo>:</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>∣</mo><mi>m</mi><mo fence=\"false\" stretchy=\"false\">}</mo></math></span>.</em></p></li>\n</ol>"],["statement:erdos-257-mersenne-support-subseries#res:period","the exact denominator period","<p><em> Let\n<span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>F</mi><mo>⊆</mo><msub><mrow><mi>ℕ</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub></math></span> be finite and\nnonempty, let <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>b</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>2</mn></math></span> be an integer,\nand let <span class=\"math inline\"><math><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>F</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></math></span> be the denominator\nof <span class=\"math inline\"><math><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>F</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></math></span> in lowest terms. Then\n<span class=\"math inline\"><math><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>F</mi></msub></math></span> is coprime to <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>b</mi></math></span>, and </em></p>\n<div class=\"math-display\"><span\nclass=\"math display\"><math display=\"block\"><msub><mi>ord</mi><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>F</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>lcm</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mo fence=\"false\" stretchy=\"false\">{</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>:</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>F</mi><mo fence=\"false\" stretchy=\"false\">}</mo><mo>.</mo></math></span></div>\n<p><em> If moreover <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>lcm</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>≥</mo><mn>2</mn></math></span>, then <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>lcm</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>F</mi></msub></math></span>. We use <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><msub><mi>ord</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math></span>, so the\nstatement includes <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>F</mi><mo>=</mo><mo fence=\"false\" stretchy=\"false\">{</mo><mn>1</mn><mo fence=\"false\" stretchy=\"false\">}</mo></math></span> at <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></math></span>.</em></p>"],["statement:erdos-257-mersenne-support-subseries#res:reciprocal-support","reciprocal-summable supports","<p><em> Let\n<span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>A</mi><mo>⊆</mo><msub><mrow><mi>ℕ</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub></math></span> be infinite. If\n</em></p>\n<div class=\"math-display\"><span class=\"math display\"><math display=\"block\"><munder><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow></munder><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>a</mi></mfrac><mo>&lt;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">∞</mi><mo>,</mo></math></span></div>\n<p class=\"display-continue\"><em>\nthen <span class=\"math inline\"><math><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></math></span> is irrational for every\ninteger <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>b</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>2</mn></math></span>.</em></p>"],["statement:erdos-257-mersenne-support-subseries#res:strict-mixed-supports","a support requiring the mixed\ncriterion","<p><em> There is an infinite positive support <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>U</mi></math></span> with <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>U</mi><mo>∉</mo><mrow><mi>𝒞</mi></mrow></math></span> and <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>U</mi><mo>∉</mo><msub><mrow><mi>𝒲</mi></mrow><mi>b</mi></msub></math></span> for every integer\n<span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>b</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>2</mn></math></span>, such that <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></math></span> is irrational for every infinite\n<span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>A</mi><mo>⊆</mo><mi>U</mi></math></span> and every integer\n<span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>b</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>2</mn></math></span>.</em></p>"],["statement:erdos-257-mersenne-support-subseries#res:terminalhalf","finite approximations with vanishing\nscaled error","<p><em> Suppose there are integers <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></math></span> tending to infinity and sets\n<span class=\"math inline\"><math><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>⊆</mo><mo fence=\"false\" stretchy=\"false\">{</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>…</mo><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo fence=\"false\" stretchy=\"false\">}</mo></math></span> such\nthat </em></p>\n<div class=\"math-display\"><span\nclass=\"math display\"><math display=\"block\"><mfrac><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">|</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">|</mo></mrow><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></msup></mfrac><mo stretchy=\"false\">⟶</mo><mn>0.</mn></math></span></div>\n<p><em>\nThen <span class=\"math inline\"><math><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></math></span> for some infinite\nset <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>A</mi><mo>⊆</mo><msub><mrow><mi>ℕ</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub></math></span>.</em></p>"],["statement:erdos-257-mersenne-support-subseries#res:weighted-cover-incomparability","incomparable support criteria","<p><em>\nThere are infinite positive supports <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>E</mi></math></span> and <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>V</mi></math></span> such that </em></p>\n<div class=\"math-display\"><span\nclass=\"math display\"><math display=\"block\"><mi>E</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mrow><mi>𝒲</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mspace width=\"1em\"></mspace><mi>E</mi><mo>∉</mo><mrow><mi>𝒞</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mspace width=\"2em\"></mspace><mi>V</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>𝒞</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mspace width=\"1em\"></mspace><mi>V</mi><mo>∉</mo><msub><mrow><mi>𝒲</mi></mrow><mi>b</mi></msub><mtext> </mtext><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>,</mo><mspace width=\"2em\"></mspace><munder><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow></munder><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>a</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">∞</mi><mo>.</mo></math></span></div>"],["statement:erdos-257-mersenne-support-subseries#res:weighted-support","a weighted condition on the support","<p><em> Let <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>b</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>2</mn></math></span> be an integer, let\n<span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>A</mi><mo>⊆</mo><msub><mrow><mi>ℕ</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub></math></span> be infinite, and\nlet <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>P</mi></math></span> be a finite nonempty set of\nprimes. Set <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><munder><mo>∏</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow></munder><msup><mi>p</mi><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow></msup></math></span>. If </em></p>\n<div class=\"math-display\"><span class=\"math display\"><math display=\"block\"><mtable minlabelspacing=\"0em\" displaystyle=\"true\"><mlabeledtr><mtd><mtext>(</mtext><mtext>1</mtext><mtext>)</mtext></mtd><mtd><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>:=</mo><munder><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow></munder><mfrac><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><msup><mi>b</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo>&lt;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">∞</mi><mo>,</mo></mtd></mlabeledtr></mtable></math></span></div>\n<p class=\"display-continue\"><em> then <span class=\"math inline\"><math><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></math></span>\nis irrational. In particular, the base-two condition </em></p>\n<div class=\"math-display\"><span\nclass=\"math display\"><math display=\"block\"><mtable minlabelspacing=\"0em\" displaystyle=\"true\"><mlabeledtr><mtd><mtext>(</mtext><mtext>W</mtext><mtext>)</mtext></mtd><mtd><munder><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow></munder><mfrac><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo>&lt;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">∞</mi></mtd></mlabeledtr></mtable></math></span></div>\n<p class=\"display-continue\"><em> implies that <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></math></span> is irrational for every integer\n<span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>b</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>2</mn></math></span>. Both conclusions are\nhereditary under passage to infinite subsets.</em></p>"],["statement:erdos-257-mersenne-support-subseries#thm:variable-fractional-cover","a summable divisor-cover criterion","<p><em>\nFor each <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>j</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></math></span>, let <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>⊆</mo><msub><mrow><mi>ℕ</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub></math></span> be finite, let <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mn>0</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn></math></span>, and let <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><msub><mi>c</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msub><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></math></span> satisfy </em></p>\n<div class=\"math-display\"><span\nclass=\"math display\"><math display=\"block\"><msub><mi>f</mi><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>n</mi><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></msup><mo>≤</mo><munder><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>∣</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></munder><msub><mi>c</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msub><mspace width=\"1em\"></mspace><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>.</mo></math></span></div>\n<p><em> Set <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><munder><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munder><msub><mi>c</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msub><mo>/</mo><mi>d</mi></math></span>. If </em></p>\n<div class=\"math-display\"><span\nclass=\"math display\"><math display=\"block\"><mtable minlabelspacing=\"0em\" displaystyle=\"true\"><mlabeledtr><mtd><mtext>(</mtext><mtext>V</mtext><mtext>)</mtext></mtd><mtd><munder><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munder><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mi>j</mi><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></msup></mrow><mrow><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>&lt;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">∞</mi><mo>,</mo></mtd></mlabeledtr></mtable></math></span></div>\n<p class=\"display-continue\"><em> then <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></math></span> is irrational for every infinite\n<span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>A</mi><mo>⊆</mo><munder><mo>⋃</mo><mi>j</mi></munder><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></math></span> and every\ninteger <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>b</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>2</mn></math></span>.</em></p>"]]}
